  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nQuiet conditions and northerly flow will persist through Tuesday\nas the coastal low tracks northeastward toward Nova Scotia. \nUpper-level ridging builds over the eastern United States by \nTuesday night, allowing low-level flow to transition to the \nsouthwest by Wednesday. This return flow will drive a noticeable\nwarming trend, with lowland daytime high temperatures surging \nback into the upper 70s and 80s for Wednesday and Thursday. \n\nA cold front will then push southward into the region Thursday\nnight and Friday. This will bring chances of showers, and\npossibly thunderstorms, to the region.",
